WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.365 --> 00:00:15.193
It almost two weeks by coach, but Jo and Beth finally arrived in California.

2
00:00:15.954 --> 00:00:21.157
Jo had reserved rooms in a small, unique hotel that also offered tours to see the wildlife, including

3
00:00:21.197 --> 00:00:28.742
buffalo. "Oh, Jo," Beth's voice shook with emotion when their tour group finally came across a herd of

4
00:00:28.802 --> 00:00:30.363
buffalo grazing on the fields.

5
00:00:31.784 --> 00:00:36.647
Just as Beth had thought, the massive creatures were gentle and peaceful as they carried on with their

6
00:00:36.667 --> 00:00:40.470
business, paying no attention to the humans staring at them from a distance.

7
00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:43.392
"Is this what you imagined them to be like?"

8
00:00:43.732 --> 00:00:44.693
Jo whispered to Beth.

9
00:00:45.593 --> 00:00:49.496
Nodding, Beth said teary eyed, "It's a dream come true.

10
00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:51.137
Thank you, Jo."

11
00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:57.701
Putting her arm around Beth's thin, weak shoulders, Jo took in every detail around her, for she wanted

12
00:00:57.721 --> 00:00:59.181
to remember this moment forever.

13
00:01:00.622 --> 00:01:05.763
After the argument with Laurie, Amy found it hard to find joy in anything, even drawing and painting.

14
00:01:06.463 --> 00:01:10.965
Laurie came by once more to tell Aunt March and her that he was leaving for Spain and

15
00:01:10.985 --> 00:01:12.665
wished them the best on the rest of their trip.

16
00:01:12.685 --> 00:01:19.487
"I think it's time for us to depart this place as well," Aunt March had said when Laurie

17
00:01:19.527 --> 00:01:21.528
left. "Where shall we go?"

18
00:01:22.012 --> 00:01:25.134
Amy asked, not really caring since she knew Laurie would not be there.

19
00:01:25.154 --> 00:01:27.696
"Florence," stated the old lady.

20
00:01:28.677 --> 00:01:33.480
But as Amy stood outside on the balcony of their villa in Florence, she felt no inspiration to

21
00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:35.782
paint one of the most beautiful cities in the world.

22
00:01:36.882 --> 00:01:38.703
All she could think about was Laurie.

23
00:01:40.245 --> 00:01:44.728
On the way back home, Jo noticed that Beth seemed to struggle more with the strenuous journey.

24
00:01:45.488 --> 00:01:50.652
She got tired easily, didn't have the energy even to look outside at the scenery, and mostly slept

25
00:01:50.712 --> 00:01:51.012
a lot.

26
00:01:51.948 --> 00:01:57.250
When they got home, Beth, barely able to stand, clung tightly to Jo's arm and said, "This has

27
00:01:57.310 --> 00:01:59.530
been the best adventure of my life, Jo.

28
00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:01.191
I'll never forget it."

29
00:02:02.511 --> 00:02:06.712
Jo clutched her hands tightly and pressed her lips to stifle an agonizing cry.

30
00:02:07.412 --> 00:02:12.494
She would have collapsed into tears then and there if not for Mother's next words, "There's a letter

31
00:02:12.574 --> 00:02:13.294
for you, Jo.

32
00:02:13.674 --> 00:02:14.474
Actually two."

33
00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:19.816
As Mother handed them over to her, Jo recognized the strong handwriting of the Professor.

34
00:02:20.668 --> 00:02:24.652
After putting Beth to bed, Jo took the letters upstairs to her sanctuary.

35
00:02:25.893 --> 00:02:27.694
As she read them, her spirits lifted.

36
00:02:28.675 --> 00:02:33.499
She even laughed as she imagined the Professor speaking aloud in his German accent and calling her "Cho."

37
00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:38.863
Holding the letters close to her chest, Jo found the strength to bear the pain that was ahead.

38
00:02:39.744 --> 00:02:42.006
A few months passed with no hope of Beth getting better.

39
00:02:42.767 --> 00:02:47.811
Without strength to sit, Beth was confined to her bed, which was moved downstairs so she could look

40
00:02:47.911 --> 00:02:49.072
out into the street and garden.

41
00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:52.481
"Jo, can you read me a story?"

42
00:02:52.761 --> 00:02:53.421
Beth would ask.

43
00:02:54.581 --> 00:02:59.042
When Jo brought over a book, Beth would move her head from side to side and say, "Leave

44
00:02:59.102 --> 00:02:59.683
me alone."

45
00:03:00.863 --> 00:03:05.144
Jo felt helpless, because she wanted to ease her sister's pain but didn't know how.

46
00:03:05.844 --> 00:03:10.325
Mother seemed to deal better with the situation, bringing things for Beth just when she needed them and

47
00:03:10.366 --> 00:03:12.246
leaving her in peace when she wanted to rest.

48
00:03:13.886 --> 00:03:19.208
Meg, who now knew that she was indeed carrying twins, also spent every day by Beth's side.

49
00:03:19.928 --> 00:03:24.771
"Feel the babies kicking, Beth," Meg would say, placing Beth's limp hand over her growing stomach.

50
00:03:24.791 --> 00:03:28.634
"I felt it, Meg," Beth would say, her eyes filling with tears.

51
00:03:29.394 --> 00:03:32.537
"You're going to be an auntie soon, darling," Meg would remind her.

52
00:03:33.697 --> 00:03:39.041
But Beth would only smile weakly and say, "I hope they're girls, and they're as beautiful as you."

53
00:03:40.042 --> 00:03:45.545
One afternoon, Jo, not wanting to disturb Beth, crept over to refill the water pitcher on the table

54
00:03:45.605 --> 00:03:46.486
next to Beth's bed.

55
00:03:46.506 --> 00:03:49.168
"Jo?" Beth called softly.

56
00:03:49.884 --> 00:03:50.604
"Yes, darling?

57
00:03:51.084 --> 00:03:51.825
Did I wake you?"

58
00:03:52.145 --> 00:03:52.685
Jo asked.

59
00:03:53.905 --> 00:03:58.306
Beth shook her head slightly as if to say no, then said, "Will you lie here with me?"

60
00:03:59.347 --> 00:04:02.868
Jo carefully got into the bed next to her sister and wrapped her arm around her.

61
00:04:02.888 --> 00:04:04.648
"I'm here, Beth.

62
00:04:05.268 --> 00:04:06.929
Do you want me to tell you a story?"

63
00:04:07.809 --> 00:04:09.650
Beth blinked her eyes once and sighed.

64
00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:13.751
"Jo? I'm ready to go now."

65
00:04:15.251 --> 00:04:21.714
Jo, not wanting to part with her sister yet, gently squeezed Beth's shoulders and said, "Hold on just

66
00:04:21.774 --> 00:04:22.814
a little longer, Beth.

67
00:04:23.354 --> 00:04:26.116
Meg's babies are coming and Amy will be home soon.

68
00:04:26.576 --> 00:04:32.618
Be strong for just a little longer But Beth turned her head, looked at her sister tenderly, then

69
00:04:32.698 --> 00:04:35.300
closed her eyes, and died in Jo's arms.

70
00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:41.202
When Beth's funeral was held a few days later, almost everyone from the town was there.

71
00:04:42.103 --> 00:04:46.612
Although the family had sent a telegram to Amy about her sister's death, they urged her to stay

72
00:04:46.652 --> 00:04:50.193
with Aunt March for the rest of the trip, because that was what Beth had wished.

73
00:04:51.954 --> 00:04:56.295
At home the March family had to rebuild their lives after the loss of beloved Beth.

74
00:04:56.855 --> 00:05:01.737
Mother, who had been so strong throughout Beth's illness, seemed to age decades in a matter of days

75
00:05:01.837 --> 00:05:05.838
afterward. Still, she found comfort in the loving arms of her husband.

76
00:05:06.558 --> 00:05:10.279
Both Mother and Father tried to give each other strength to cope with the loss of one of

77
00:05:10.319 --> 00:05:10.859
their children.

78
00:05:12.059 --> 00:05:13.640
However, Jo was inconsolable.

79
00:05:14.268 --> 00:05:17.430
No amount of kind words or deeds could soothe the pain in her heart.

80
00:05:18.371 --> 00:05:23.494
Every day she escaped into the woods, taking long walks by herself with her memories of her sweet

81
00:05:23.554 --> 00:05:29.358
sister. A few weeks after Beth's death, Jo was just clearing up the dishes from dinner when John

82
00:05:29.418 --> 00:05:30.459
came running into the house.

83
00:05:30.479 --> 00:05:34.502
"Please, come quickly," he said breathlessly.

84
00:05:34.522 --> 00:05:36.303
"Meg is having the babies!"

85
00:05:37.143 --> 00:05:41.206
Mother, Father, Jo, and Hannah raced out, leaving the dishes and other worries behind.

86
00:05:42.767 --> 00:05:44.448
When they got to the house, Dr.

87
00:05:44.488 --> 00:05:46.669
Bangs and a midwife were already there with Meg.

88
00:05:47.469 --> 00:05:51.951
Mother went into the room with them while Jo, John, and Father paced the living room anxiously.

89
00:05:52.992 --> 00:05:55.153
A few hours later, they heard a baby crying.

90
00:05:55.173 --> 00:05:57.434
"Oh John!"

91
00:05:57.834 --> 00:06:00.375
Jo cried, holding onto her brother-in-law's hand.

92
00:06:00.395 --> 00:06:08.998
"Congratulations!" Then shortly after, another cry erupted, and they could hear laughter and cries from behind the door.

93
00:06:09.018 --> 00:06:11.419
"John?" Dr.

94
00:06:11.459 --> 00:06:12.660
Bangs called, opening the door.

95
00:06:13.208 --> 00:06:14.368
"Come in and see your babies.

96
00:06:14.748 --> 00:06:15.209
Come, Mr.

97
00:06:15.229 --> 00:06:16.869
March. You too, Jo and Hannah."

98
00:06:17.969 --> 00:06:22.350
Everyone crowded into the room where Meg sat up holding one baby in the crook of each arm.

99
00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:28.192
"This is your new son," she said, looking at the bundle on her right, then pointed her chin

100
00:06:28.292 --> 00:06:30.773
toward the left, adding, "and your new daughter."

101
00:06:31.733 --> 00:06:36.314
Everyone started hugging and crying as they welcomed the newest members of the family into the world.

102
00:06:37.635 --> 00:06:41.896
Jo looked lovingly at her niece and nephew and realized for a sad moment that they would never

103
00:06:41.936 --> 00:06:42.736
see their Aunt Beth.

104
00:06:43.392 --> 00:06:48.438
However, Jo promised to do what she could to help them get acquainted with the wonderful aunt who

105
00:06:48.478 --> 00:06:49.780
had died before their birth.

106
00:06:50.441 --> 00:06:51.982
"What are you going to name them, Meg?

107
00:06:52.563 --> 00:06:53.805
John?" asked Father.

108
00:06:53.825 --> 00:06:57.229
"Daisy and Demi," the happy parents said together.

109
00:06:57.249 --> 00:07:01.494
"Welcome to your family," the new grandfather said proudly.
